Single-binary distribution epic 6f11d483, step 4 (issue 50afbc47).

- Add scripts/install.sh (POSIX): detects os/arch/libc, maps to the
  release asset, downloads from GitHub Releases (latest or --version),
  installs to ~/.local/bin/forge with a PATH note. Hidden --print-asset
  mode makes the mapping unit-testable.
- Add scripts/install.ps1 (PowerShell) for windows-x64: downloads
  forge-windows-x64.exe to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\forge.
- Add scripts/lib/release-asset.mjs: canonical os/arch/libc -> asset
  mapping (single source of truth for all 7 targets).
- Add scripts/release-asset.test.js: covers all 7 targets and
  cross-checks install.sh --print-asset against the JS contract.
- Wire a Release-upload job into .github/workflows/build-binary.yml:
  on v* tags, download the build artifacts, strip the internal bun-
  prefix to clean forge-<os>-<arch>[-musl][.exe] asset names, and
  gh release upload them (Step 3 was artifact-only).
- Add docs/reference/INSTALL.md (one-line install, manual download,
  supported-platforms table, npm/npx alternative, prerequisites);
  link it from README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
